## 1. `Assets/Scripts/Bezier/linerendeler.cs`
**Path:** `D:\UnityProject\air1\Assets\Scripts\Bezier\linerendeler.cs`

A `[RequireComponent(typeof(LineRenderer))]` class that draws a Catmull-Rom spline between two port anchors with three on-curve handles (20%/50%/80%).

**How p0/p2 are set:** `p0` and `p2` are `public Transform` fields (the two endpoint port anchors). They are NOT set internally — they are assigned externally by `TubeBuilderManager.CreateTube()`:
```csharp
var oldBezier = newTube.GetComponent<linerendeler>();
if (oldBezier != null) {
    oldBezier.p0 = firstJoint;   // first selected PortBase transform
    oldBezier.p2 = secondJoint;  // second selected PortBase transform
}
```

**How RegisterConnection works (the only "registration" mechanism here):**
```csharp
private portandvalve _wirePortA, _wirePortB;
private PortBase _wireBaseA, _wireBaseB;
private bool isConnectionRegistered = false;

private void RegisterConnection() {
    if (SimulationLoop.Instance == null || p0 == null || p2 == null) return;
    PortBase portA = p0.GetComponent<PortBase>();
    PortBase portB = p2.GetComponent<PortBase>();
    if (portA != null && portB != null) {
        // Cache data so even if p0/p2 destroyed, cached refs still locate for unregister
        _wirePortA = portA.portandvalve;
        _wirePortB = portB.portandvalve;
        _wireBaseA = portA;
        _wireBaseB = portB;
        SimulationLoop.Instance.RegisterWire(portA, portB);
        isConnectionRegistered = true;
    } else {
        Debug.LogWarning("管线两端的接口缺少 PortBase 组件，无法注册线缆！");
    }
}

private void UnregisterConnection() {
    if (isConnectionRegistered && SimulationLoop.Instance != null) {
        SimulationLoop.Instance.UnregisterWire(_wireBaseA, _wireBaseB);
        isConnectionRegistered = false;
        _wireBaseA = null; _wireBaseB = null;
    }
}
```

**Where RegisterConnection is called:** Inside `Update()`, gated by a one-time `isInitialized` flag that fires once `p0`/`p2` have a real distance > 0.01f (deferred init to avoid both anchors co-located at spawn):
```csharp
if (!isInitialized && Vector3.Distance(p0.position, p2.position) > 0.01f) {
    InitializeHandlesCurved();
    RegisterConnection();   // register connection when curve initializes
    isInitialized = true;
}
```
**Note:** `RegisterConnection` is invoked automatically by `Update()` — there is no explicit `SetConnection`/`Setup` method on this class; it self-initializes from the externally-assigned `p0`/`p2`.

**Wire endpoints (PortBase) determination:** Endpoints come from `p0.GetComponent<PortBase>()` and `p2.GetComponent<PortBase>()` at registration time. On `OnDestroy()`, it calls `UnregisterConnection()` plus a double-null-check disconnect of both ports (handles Unity "fake null" after `DeleteAllValves`):
```csharp
PortBase portA = (p0 != null) ? p0.GetComponent<PortBase>() : null;
PortBase portB = (p2 != null) ? p2.GetComponent<PortBase>() : null;
if (portA != null && portB != null) { portA.Disconnect(); portB.Disconnect(); }
```
The curve uses 5 control points (`p0, handle20, handle50, handle80, p2`) and `InitializeHandlesCurved()` places handles using parabolic weight `4*t*(1-t)` for a natural U-shape droop via `defaultCurveOffset` (default `(0.5,0,0.5)`).

---

## 2. `Assets/Scripts/Bezier/TubeBuilderManager.cs`
**Path:** `D:\UnityProject\air1\Assets\Scripts\Bezier\TubeBuilderManager.cs`

A singleton (`Instance`) that builds tubes/wires between two selected ports. Full flow from StartBuild to wire completion:

**Entry points (UI buttons):**
```csharp
public void StartBuildPneumaticTube()   { StartBuildTube("pneumatic"); }
public void StartBuildtinckwireTube()   { StartBuildTube("tinckElec"); }   // xixian (thin wire)
public void StartBuildwireTube()        { StartBuildTube("simplleElec"); } // cuxian (thick wire)
```

**Prefabs stored:** `pneumaticPrefab`, `xixianPrefab` (thin elec), `cuxianPrefab` (thick elec) — all GameObjects "带有 BezierRendererInverse 脚本".

**StartBuildTube(string tubeType):** Ends any current selection, sets `isSelecting=true`, clears `firstJoint`/`secondJoint`, parses `tubeType` into `CurrentjointChanel` enum via `Enum.Parse`, finds all GameObjects with that tag, and highlights (via `HighlightEffect`) every joint whose `PortBase` is free (not occupied, or stackable). Warns if fewer than 2 joints found.

**Update() selection loop:** Only runs while `isSelecting`. Skips clicks on real UI (Layer 5). Raycasts from camera; if hit transform's tag matches `CurrentjointChanel.ToString()`, calls `HandleJointSelection(hit.transform)`.

**HandleJointSelection:** Rejects if port exists, not stackable, and already occupied. Sets `firstJoint` if null; otherwise sets `secondJoint` (must differ from first) and calls `CreateTube()`.

**CreateTube() — full wire completion flow:**
```csharp
private void CreateTube() {
    GameObject newTube = null;
    switch (CurrentjointChanel) {
        case portChanel.pneumatic:   newTube = Instantiate(pneumaticPrefab); break;
        case portChanel.tinckElec:   newTube = Instantiate(xixianPrefab); break;   // DynamicWire
        case portChanel.simplleElec: newTube = Instantiate(cuxianPrefab); break;   // DynamicWire
    }
    if (newTube == null) return;
    newTube.transform.position = Vector3.zero;

    PortBase portA = firstJoint.GetComponent<PortBase>();
    PortBase portB = secondJoint.GetComponent<PortBase>();

    // Core compatibility split: electrical wires vs pneumatic tubes
    if (CurrentjointChanel == portChanel.tinckElec || CurrentjointChanel == portChanel.simplleElec) {
        DynamicWire wireTopology = newTube.GetComponent<DynamicWire>();
        if (wireTopology != null && portA != null && portB != null) {
            wireTopology.SetupWire(portA.circuitNode, portB.circuitNode);
        } else { Debug.LogError("电线预制体上未找到 DynamicWire 脚本，或接口缺失！"); }
    } else {
        // pneumatic: legacy bezier assignment
        var oldBezier = newTube.GetComponent<linerendeler>();
        if (oldBezier != null) { oldBezier.p0 = firstJoint; oldBezier.p2 = secondJoint; }
    }

    // Bind physical port state
    if (portA != null && portB != null) {
        portA.OnConnect(portB); portB.OnConnect(portA);
        portA.isOccupied = true; portB.isOccupied = true;
    }
    EndSelection();
