## Cross-file wiring summary (the requested flow)
- **Spawn/place items:** `UI_TestPanelItemBTN.Init(Item, num)` sets `_gridObjectToSpawnPrefab = Item.prefab` (Item defined in `ItemManager.cs`). `UseItem()` instantiates it, attaches/links `Item3D` (`itemUI=this`, `itemSelf=itemins`), enters grid placement. On grid placement, `Item3D.hasCreate` gates a one-time decrement of `itemnum`/increment of `chazhi`.
- **Build wires:** `TubeBuilderManager.StartBuildTube(tag)` highlights free `PortBase` joints of that channel; player picks two → `CreateTube()` instantiates `pneumaticPrefab`/`xixianPrefab`/`cuxianPrefab`. Electrical wires use `DynamicWire.SetupWire(portA.circuitNode, portB.circuitNode)`; pneumatic tubes assign `linerendeler.p0`/`p2` to the two joints, then both ports get `OnConnect` + `isOccupied=true`.
- **Wire endpoint tracking:** `linerendeler` derives its two `PortBase` endpoints from `p0.GetComponent<PortBase>()` / `p2.GetComponent<PortBase>()` during its deferred `Update()` init, caches them, and calls `SimulationLoop.Instance.RegisterWire(portA, portB)`. On destroy it `UnregisterWire(...)` and calls `Disconnect()` on both ports.

